s="r-14d8ftz" loading="eager"/></picture><div data-rid="8948d130-bc7c-4c89-b18c-90b453b166b6" class="r-11z7n9b alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>600k+ Likes</p></span></div></div><div data-rid="4dc58c03-50b2-4f32-b136-8a84600c4945" class="r-w6tdrt"><picture data-rid="4ec5a4ef-0e0f-440c-868b-86dc60209a05" class="r-st9x99"><img src="https://andytown-public.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/templates/component-templates/Onnit-advert.json/63eb24ccca797b36c69f0c8e_about09.png%3Fv%3D1678390871" class="r-1hcbsyr" loading="eager"/></picture><div data-rid="9b15124a-7846-4750-a67d-e85ebf7e36fb" class="r-f8l850 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>160k+ Followers</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="bcc2d58f-0773-4d46-903e-ba90b7708b9a" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="The Answer" tabindex="-1" id="The Answer" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-2gco1m"><div data-rid="77b1a4f1-9dd3-4018-8673-8e06d56f4d5b" class="r-1dyogz6 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong><mark data-color="#FAF8D9FF" style="background-color: #FAF8D9FF; color: inherit">My Doctor Laughed at This Remedy Mentioned in the Quran—Until He Saw My Results</mark></strong></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I still remember when my doctor gave me the news I dreaded.</span></p><p><br><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"Your blood sugar levels are climbing. We need to start you on medication."</span></em></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I hesitated, hoping for a natural solution—one without side effects.</span></p><p><strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"Is there any way I can manage this without pills?"</span></em></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> I asked.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">He sighed, flipping through my chart. </span><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"Look, diet and exercise help, but this is just how diabetes progresses. You don’t want to wait until it gets worse."</span></em></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I wasn’t against medicine, but I didn’t want to rely on pills for life. So I asked, </span><strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"What about natural remedies? Something like black seed oil?"</span></em></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">That’s when he chuckled. </span></strong></p><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"><br></span><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"If that stuff worked, we’d be prescribing it already."</span></em></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I felt embarrassed, but deep down, I wasn’t convinced. I had heard about the </span><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">benefits of black seed oil and honey from my mother growing up</span></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">, but I had never taken it seriously.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I left his office disappointed—but determined to find answers.</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="418b228f-513c-429e-8a46-4106841305b6" class="r-1y2xpyc"><div data-rid="dffb290c-cd4e-40ef-9f9b-ade9f11cbef1" class="r-1wlm5gg alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The Answer Was in the Quran—But I Had Overlooked It</p></span></div></div><picture data-rid="b4375aba-6281-4405-8cb1-e181ade66db5" class="r-13ac83t"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7c1cab82-e9a7-4f98-b8a0-d351d5fbba11?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7c1cab82-e9a7-4f98-b8a0-d351d5fbba11?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7c1cab82-e9a7-4f98-b8a0-d351d5fbba11?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7c1cab82-e9a7-4f98-b8a0-d351d5fbba11" class="r-v3ig3" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="363adfd5-8d25-4b97-aebd-d4c6d9904c6b" class="r-1tvlrw7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">A few weeks later, I traveled to </span><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Karachi</span></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> for a family wedding. My health was the last thing on my mind—I was just happy to be home, surrounded by family and good food.</span></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">One evening, after dinner, my uncle pulled me aside.</span></em></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"You’ve been drinking water constantly. Do you wake up at night too?"</span></em></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I paused. How did he notice?</span></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"And you feel exhausted after meals, hai na?" he continued.</span></em></p><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I nodded, still wondering how he knew.</span></em></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">For a moment, I hesitated. But something about the way he spoke—</span></em><strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">the concern in his voice, the way he had noticed what even I had ignored—made me feel safe enough to share.</span></em></strong></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I told him everything. The rising blood sugar, the doctor’s insistence on medication, and the way he had laughed when I mentioned black seed oil.</span></em></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">My uncle shook his head.</span><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> "People put their trust in science alone and forget that </span></em><strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Allah (SWT) has already provided healing."</span></em></strong></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">He disappeared into the kitchen and returned with a bottle of black seed oil and a jar of honey.</span></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"</span></em><strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">This is Sunnah,"</span></em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> he said, pouring a spoonful of black seed oil into a cup. </span><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"The Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) said black seed is a cure for every disease except death." </span></em></strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">(Sahih al-Bukhari)</span></em></p></span></div><div data-rid="88139a27-a746-465a-ba0c-c3c6cea8dc67" class="r-wj2kps alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I had always known about black seed oil, but I had never taken it consistently.</span></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"Take a spoon of this oil with honey every morning,"</span></em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> he said.</span><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> </span><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"But also, make du’a. Trust in what Allah (SWT) has given us."</span></em></strong></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I wasn’t sure it would work, but I trusted my uncle’s wisdom.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">So I started taking it—and I started praying.</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="c9c14889-a418-40d8-a484-f8d3acc9ee3f" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="Black Seed" tabindex="-1" id="Black Seed" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-gjqmct"><div data-rid="9cbe6612-6399-40fb-bb9e-3b9f36f37532" class="r-11z1lm8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Black Seed Oil Worked—But Taking It Was a Struggle</p></span></div><picture data-rid="7ce802ec-42ac-4471-8673-4d11cd979d7c" class="r-1id8lv2"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/f17c41d6-bbb0-42a3-83ff-de7f30947e64?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/f17c41d6-bbb0-42a3-83ff-de7f30947e64?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/f17c41d6-bbb0-42a3-83ff-de7f30947e64?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/f17c41d6-bbb0-42a3-83ff-de7f30947e64" class="r-mhjabs" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div data-rid="b6e033c0-9e33-4191-992d-472828b9d14e" class="r-1vecg9 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">When I got back home, I stuck to my uncle’s advice—black seed oil and honey every morning.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">And it worked—I had more energy, no more constant thirst, no crashes after meals. But taking it? Bitter. Thick. Messy. Some days, I skipped it just to avoid the hassle.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Then I got lazy. Missed a few days. Then a few more. By the end of the week, the exhaustion crept back. </span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">The thirst. The sluggishness. I knew black seed oil worked—but sticking with it was the hard part.</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="dae569a9-29b6-4dbc-9d4d-196970467b1f" class="r-oy4ckl alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>I finally found a better way.</strong></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">This was a gummy supplement with black seed oil and honey—same prophetic ingredients, just easier.</span></p><br><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">No bitterness, no mess, no struggle.</span></strong></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I gave it a try, and for once, sticking with it was easy. Within days, I felt the difference—like I had my health back again.</span></p><br><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Then, I met my doctor again.</span></p></span></div><div data-rid="885cd9d1-ae2b-42f1-a208-b3aed5d30273" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="Miracle" tabindex="-1" id="Miracle" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-v22i8g"><div data-rid="b9d4b28a-79fd-45ef-b58e-d5bdd0961c7f" class="r-mbhmyy alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>"This Is Nothing Short of a Miracle."</p></span></div><picture data-rid="c4b87fee-ce56-4c81-ba4c-ade0b7d1cfc4" class="r-cxccwo"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7b0b2795-5e78-44c9-92cf-41659412bba5?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7b0b2795-5e78-44c9-92cf-41659412bba5?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7b0b2795-5e78-44c9-92cf-41659412bba5?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/26af2a77-1069-4b08-aa49-d5a2611869f6/7b0b2795-5e78-44c9-92cf-41659412bba5" class="r-r6u761" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div data-rid="d6bd0e19-37a9-4b0d-8a5e-f895a2f5866f" class="r-1eg09l0 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I sat across from him as he flipped through my test results, his brows furrowing. He double-checked the numbers, then shook his head.</span></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"This... this is incredible,"</span></em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> he muttered, shaking his head.</span></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"</span></em><strong><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">Honestly, this is nothing short of a miracle."</span></em></strong></p><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"Your blood sugar levels are completely stable. What medication did you take?"</span></em></p><br><p><em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">"None,"</span></em><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)"> I said, barely holding back a smile.</span></p><p><strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">I told him about black seed oil and honey</span></strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0)">—how I had taken it daily, how I had switched to a